H0800.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 784;
Meaning: fire
KJV renders: fire.

H0801.strongs:
Origin: the same as 800, but used in a liturgical sense;
Meaning: properly, a burnt-offering; but occasionally of any sacrifice
KJV renders: (offering, sacrifice), (made) by fire.

H0803.strongs:
Origin: feminine passive participle from an unused root meaning to found;
Meaning: foundation
KJV renders: foundation.

H0804.strongs:
Origin: or אַשֻּׁר; apparently from 833 (in the sense of successful);
Meaning: Ashshur, the second son of Shem; also his descendants and the country occupied by them (i.e. Assyria), its region and its empire
KJV renders: Asshur, Assur, Assyria, Assyrians. See 838.

H0805.strongs:
Origin: or אַשּׁוּרִי; from a patrial word of the same form as 804;
Meaning: an Ashurite (collectively) or inhabitant of Ashur, a district in Palestine
KJV renders: Asshurim, Ashurites.

H0806.strongs:
Origin: probably from 7835; black;
Meaning: Ashchur, an Israelite
KJV renders: Ashur.

H0807.strongs:
Origin: of foreign origin;
Meaning: Ashima, a deity of Hamath
KJV renders: Ashima.

H0808.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 784 (in the sense of pressing down firmly; compare 803);
Meaning: a (ruined) foundation
KJV renders: foundation.

H0809.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 808;
Meaning: something closely pressed together, i.e. a cake of raisins or other comfits
KJV renders: flagon.

H0810.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (probably meaning to bunch together);
Meaning: a testicle (as a lump)
KJV renders: stone.

H0811.strongs:
Origin: or אֶשְׁכֹּל; probably prolonged from 810;
Meaning: a bunch of grapes or other fruit
KJV renders: cluster (of grapes).

H0812.strongs:
Origin: the same as 811;
Meaning: Eshcol, the name of an Amorite, also of a valley in Palestine
KJV renders: Eshcol.

H0813.strongs:
Origin: of foreign origin;
Meaning: Ashkenaz, a Japhethite, also his descendants
KJV renders: Ashkenaz.

H0814.strongs:
Origin: for 7939;
Meaning: a gratuity
KJV renders: gift, present.

H0815.strongs:
Origin: from a root of uncertain signification;
Meaning: a tamarisk tree; by extension, a grove of any kind
KJV renders: grove, tree.

H0816.strongs:
Origin: or אָשֵׁם; a primitive root;
Meaning: to be guilty; by implication to be punished or perish
KJV renders: × certainly, be(-come, made) desolate, destroy, × greatly, be(-come, found, hold) guilty, offend (acknowledge offence), trespass.

H0817.strongs:
Origin: from 816;
Meaning: guilt; by implication, a fault; also a sin-offering
KJV renders: guiltiness, (offering for) sin, trespass (offering).

H0818.strongs:
Origin: from 816;
Meaning: guilty; hence, presenting a sin-offering
KJV renders: one which is faulty, guilty.

H0819.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 817;
Meaning: guiltiness, a fault, the presentation of a sin-offering
KJV renders: offend, sin, (cause of) trespass(-ing, offering).

H0820.strongs:
Origin: probably from 8081;
Meaning: a fat field
KJV renders: desolate place.

H0821.strongs:
Origin: or אַשׁמוּרָה; or אַשׁמֹרֶת; (feminine) from 8104;
Meaning: a night watch
KJV renders: watch.

H0822.strongs:
Origin: apparently from an unused root (probably meaning to leave interstices);
Meaning: a latticed window
KJV renders: casement, lattice.

H0823.strongs:
Origin: probably a variation for 3466;
Meaning: Ashnah, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV renders: Ashnah.

H0824.strongs:
Origin: from 8172; support;
Meaning: Eshan, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Eshean.

H0825.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (probably meaning to lisp, i.e. practice enchantment);
Meaning: a conjurer
KJV renders: astrologer.

H0827.strongs:
Origin: perhaps (feminine) from the same as 825 (in the sense of covering);
Meaning: a quiver or arrow-case
KJV renders: quiver.

H0828.strongs:
Origin: of foreign origin;
Meaning: Ashpenaz, a Babylonian eunuch
KJV renders: Ashpenaz.

H0829.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: a measured portion
KJV renders: good piece (of flesh).

H0830.strongs:
Origin: or אַשְׁפּוֹת; or שְׁפֹת; (contraction) plural of a noun of the same form as 827, from 8192 (in the sense of scraping);
Meaning: a heap of rubbish or filth
KJV renders: dung (hill).

H0831.strongs:
Origin: probably from 8254 in the sense of weighing-place (i.e. mart);
Meaning: Ashkelon, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Ashkelon, Askalon.

H0832.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 831;
Meaning: Ashkelonite (collectively) or inhabitant of Ashkelon
KJV renders: Eshkalonites.

H0833.strongs:
Origin: or אָשֵׁר; a primitive root;
Meaning: to be straight (used in the widest sense, especially to be level, right, happy); figuratively, to go forward, be honest, prosper
KJV renders: (call, be) bless(-ed, happy), go, guide, lead, relieve.

H0834.strongs:
Origin: a primitive relative pronoun (of every gender and number);
Meaning: who, which, what, that; also (as an adverb and a conjunction) when, where, how, because, in order that, etc.
KJV renders: × after, × alike, as (soon as), because, × every, for, + forasmuch, + from whence, + how(-soever), × if, (so) that ((thing) which, wherein), × though, + until, + whatsoever, when, where (+ -as, -in, -of, -on, -soever, -with), which, whilst, + whither(-soever), who(-m, -soever, -se). As it is indeclinable, it is often accompanied by the personal pronoun expletively, used to show the connection.

H0835.strongs:
Origin: from 833;
Meaning: happiness; only in masculine plural construction as interjection, how happy!
KJV renders: blessed, happy.

H0836.strongs:
Origin: from 833, happy;
Meaning: Asher, a son of Jacob, and the tribe descended from him, with its territory; also a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Asher

H0837.strongs:
Origin: from 833;
Meaning: happiness
KJV renders: happy.

H0838.strongs:
Origin: or אַשֻּׁר; from 833 in the sense of going;
Meaning: a step
KJV renders: going, step.

H0839.strongs:
Origin: contracted for 8391;
Meaning: the cedar tree or some other light elastic wood
KJV renders: Ashurite.

H0840.strongs:
Origin: by orthographical variation from 833 and 410; right of God;
Meaning: Asarel, an Israelite
KJV renders: Asareel.

H0841.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 840; right toward God;
Meaning: Asarelah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Asarelah. Compare 3480.

H0842.strongs:
Origin: or אֲשֵׁירָה; from 833; happy;
Meaning: Asherah (or Astarte) a Phoenician goddess; also an image of the same
KJV renders: grove. Compare 6253.

H0843.strongs:
Origin: patronymic from 836;
Meaning: an Asherite (collectively) or descendant of Asher
KJV renders: Asherites.

H0844.strongs:
Origin: an orthographical variation for 840;
Meaning: Asriel, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Ashriel, Asriel.

H0845.strongs:
Origin: patronymic from 844;
Meaning: an Asrielite (collectively) or descendant of Asriel
KJV renders: Asrielites.

H0846.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to 833;
Meaning: a wall (from its uprightness)
KJV renders: wall.

H0847.strongs:
Origin: or אֶשְׁתָּאוֹל; probably from 7592; intreaty;
Meaning: Eshtaol, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Eshtaol.

H0848.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 847;
Meaning: an Eshtaolite (collectively) or inhabitant of Eshtaol
KJV renders: Eshtaulites.

H0849.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from 7712 (in a bad sense);
Meaning: rebellion
KJV renders: sedition.

H0850.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same as 7764; restful;
Meaning: Eshton, an Israelite
KJV renders: Eshton.

H0851.strongs:
Origin: or אֶשְׁתְּמוֹעַ; or אֶשְׁתְּמֹה; from 8085 (in the sense of obedience);
Meaning: Eshtemoa or Eshtemoh, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Eshtemoa, Eshtemoh.

H0852.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 226;
Meaning: a portent
KJV renders: sign.

H0853.strongs:
Origin: apparent contracted from 226 in the demonstrative sense of entity;
Meaning: properly, self (but generally used to point out more definitely the object of a verb or preposition, even or namely)
KJV renders: [as such unrepresented in English].

H0854.strongs:
Origin: probably from 579;
Meaning: properly, nearness (used only as a preposition or an adverb), near; hence, generally, with, by, at, among, etc.
KJV renders: against, among, before, by, for, from, in(-to), (out) of, with. Often with another prepositional prefix.

H0855.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: a hoe or other digging implement
KJV renders: coulter, plowshare.

H0856.strongs:
Origin: from 854 and 1168; with Baal;
Meaning: Ethbaal, a Phoenician king
KJV renders: Ethbaal.

H0857.strongs:
Origin: or אָתָא; a primitive root (collateral to 225 contraction);
Meaning: to arrive
KJV renders: (be-, things to) come (upon), bring.

H0859.strongs:
Origin: or (shortened); אַתָּ; or אַת; feminine (irregular) sometimes אַתִּי; plural masculine אַתֶּם; feminine אַתֶּן; or אַתֵּנָהlemma אתֵּנָה missing vowel, corrected to אַתֵּנָה; or אַתֵּנָּה; a primitive pronoun of the second person;
Meaning: thou and thee, or (plural) ye and you
KJV renders: thee, thou, ye, you.

H0860.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same as 386 (in the sense of patience);
Meaning: a female donkey (from its docility)
KJV renders: (she) ass.

H0861.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) probably from the corresponding to 784;
Meaning: probably a fire-place, i.e. furnace
KJV renders: furnace.

H0862.strongs:
Origin: or אַתִּיק; from 5423 in the sense of decreasing;
Meaning: a ledge or offset in a building
KJV renders: gallery.

H0863.strongs:
Origin: or אִיתַי; from 854; near;
Meaning: Ittai or Ithai, the name of a Gittite and of an Israelite
KJV renders: Ithai, Ittai.

H0864.strongs:
Origin: of Egyptian derivation;
Meaning: Etham, a place in the Desert
KJV renders: Etham.

H0865.strongs:
Origin: or אִתְמוֹל; or אֶתְמוּל; probably from 853 or 854 and 4136;
Meaning: heretofore; definitely yesterday
KJV renders: before (that) time, heretofore, of late (old), times past, yester(day).

H0866.strongs:
Origin: from 8566;
Meaning: a present (as the price of harlotry)
KJV renders: reward.

H0867.strongs:
Origin: perhaps from 866; munificence;
Meaning: Ethni, an Israelite
KJV renders: Ethni.

H0868.strongs:
Origin: the same as 866;
Meaning: a gift (as the price of harlotry or idolatry)
KJV renders: hire, reward.

H0869.strongs:
Origin: the same as 868 in the sense of 867;
Meaning: Ethnan, an Israelite
KJV renders: Ethnan.

H0870.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of 871;
Meaning: a place; (adverb) after
KJV renders: after, place.

H0871.strongs:
Origin: plural from an unused root (probably meaning to step); places;
Meaning: Atharim, a place near Palestine
KJV renders: spies. b

H0872.strongs:
Origin: from 935;
Meaning: an entrance to a building
KJV renders: entry.

H0873.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from 888;
Meaning: wicked
KJV renders: bad.

H0874.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to dig; by analogy, to engrave; figuratively, to explain
KJV renders: declare, (make) plain(-ly).

H0875.strongs:
Origin: from 874;
Meaning: a pit; especially a well
KJV renders: pit, well.

H0876.strongs:
Origin: the same as 875;
Meaning: Beer, a place in the Desert, also one in Palestine
KJV renders: Beer.

H0877.strongs:
Origin: from 874;
Meaning: a cistern
KJV renders: cistern.

H0878.strongs:
Origin: from 875; a well;
Meaning: Beera, an Israelite
KJV renders: Beera.

H0879.strongs:
Origin: from 875 and the plural of 410; well of heroes;
Meaning: Beer-Elim, a place in the Desert
KJV renders: Beer-elim.

H0880.strongs:
Origin: the same as 878;
Meaning: Beerah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Beerah.

H0881.strongs:
Origin: feminine plural of 875; wells;
Meaning: Beeroth, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Beeroth.

H0882.strongs:
Origin: from 875; fountained;
Meaning: Beeri, the name of a Hittite and of an Israelite
KJV renders: Beeri.

H0883.strongs:
Origin: from 875 and 2416 (with prefix) and 7203; well of a living (One) my Seer;
Meaning: Beer-Lachai-Roi, a place in the Desert
KJV renders: Beer-lahai-roi.

H0884.strongs:
Origin: from 875 and 7651 (in the sense of 7650); well of an oath;
Meaning: Beer-Sheba, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Beer-shebah.

H0885.strongs:
Origin: from the feminine plural of 875, and the plural contraction of 1121, and 3292; wells of (the) sons of Jaakan;
Meaning: Beeroth-Bene-Jaakan, a place in the Desert
KJV renders: Beeroth of the children of Jaakan.

H0886.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 881;
Meaning: a Beerothite or inhabitant of Beeroth
KJV renders: Beerothite.

H0887.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to smell bad; figuratively, to be offensive morally
KJV renders: (make to) be abhorred (had in abomination, loathsome, odious), (cause a, make to) stink(-ing savour), × utterly.

H0889.strongs:
Origin: from 877;
Meaning: a stench
KJV renders: stink.

H0890.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 889;
Meaning: stink-weed or any other noxious or useless plant
KJV renders: cockle.

H0891.strongs:
Origin: plural of 889;
Meaning: poison-berries
KJV renders: wild grapes.

H0892.strongs:
Origin: feminine active participle of an unused root meaning to hollow out;
Meaning: something hollowed (as a gate), i.e. pupil of the eye
KJV renders: apple (of the eye).

H0893.strongs:
Origin: probably of foreign origin;
Meaning: Bebai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Bebai.

H0894.strongs:
Origin: from 1101; confusion;
Meaning: Babel (i.e. Babylon), including Babylonia and the Babylonian empire
KJV renders: Babel, Babylon.

H0896.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) patrial from 895;
Meaning: a Babylonian
KJV renders: Babylonia.

H0897.strongs:
Origin: a Persian word;
Meaning: food
KJV renders: spoil (from the margin for 957.)

H0898.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to cover (with a garment); figuratively, to act covertly; by implication, to pillage
KJV renders: deal deceitfully (treacherously, unfaithfully), offend, transgress(-or), (depart), treacherous (dealer, -ly, man), unfaithful(-ly, man), × very.

H0899.strongs:
Origin: from 898;
Meaning: a covering, i.e. clothing; also treachery or pillage
KJV renders: apparel, cloth(-es, ing), garment, lap, rag, raiment, robe, × very (treacherously), vesture, wardrobe.

H0900.strongs:
Origin: feminine plural active participle of 898;
Meaning: treacheries
KJV renders: treacherous.

H0901.strongs:
Origin: from 898;
Meaning: treacherous
KJV renders: treacherous.

H0902.strongs:
Origin: probably of foreign origin;
Meaning: Bigvai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Bigvai.

H0903.strongs:
Origin: of Persian derivation;
Meaning: Bigtha, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV renders: Bigtha.

H0904.strongs:
Origin: or בִּגְתָנָא; of similar derivation to 903;
Meaning: Bigthan or Bigthana, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV renders: Bigthan, Bigthana.

H0905.strongs:
Origin: from 909;
Meaning: properly, separation; by implication, a part of the body, branch of a tree, bar for carrying; figuratively, chief of a city; especially (with prepositional prefix) as an adverb, apart, only, besides
KJV renders: alone, apart, bar, besides, branch, by self, of each alike, except, only, part, staff, strength.

H0906.strongs:
Origin: perhaps from 909 (in the sense of divided fibres);
Meaning: flaxen thread or yarn; hence, a linen garment
KJV renders: linen.

H0907.strongs:
Origin: from 908;
Meaning: a brag or lie; also a liar
KJV renders: liar, lie.

H0908.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: (figuratively) to invent
KJV renders: devise, feign.

H0909.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to divide, i.e. (reflex.) be solitary
KJV renders: alone.

H0910.strongs:
Origin: from 909;
Meaning: separate; adverb, separately
KJV renders: alone, desolate, only, solitary.

H0911.strongs:
Origin: from 909; separation;
Meaning: Bedad, an Edomite
KJV renders: Bedad.

H0912.strongs:
Origin: probably a shortened form 5662; servant of Jehovah;
Meaning: Bedejah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Bedeiah.

H0913.strongs:
Origin: from 914;
Meaning: alloy (because removed by smelting); by analogy, tin
KJV renders: plummet, tin.

H0914.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to divide (in variation senses literally or figuratively, separate, distinguish, differ, select, etc.)
KJV renders: (make, put) difference, divide (asunder), (make) separate (self, -ation), sever (out), × utterly.

H0915.strongs:
Origin: from 914;
Meaning: a part
KJV renders: piece.

H0916.strongs:
Origin: probably from 914;
Meaning: something in pieces, i.e. bdellium, a (fragrant) gum (perhaps amber); others a pearl
KJV renders: bdellium.

H0917.strongs:
Origin: probably shortened for 5658; servile;
Meaning: Bedan, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Bedan.

H0918.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root; to gap open; used only as a denominative from 919;
Meaning: to mend a breach
KJV renders: repair.

H0919.strongs:
Origin: from 918;
Meaning: a gap or leak (in a building or a ship)
KJV renders: breach, calker.

H0920.strongs:
Origin: probably from 1856 with a prepositional prefix; by stabbing, i.e. assassin;
Meaning: Bidkar, an Israelite
KJV renders: Bidkar.

H0921.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding (by transposition) to 6504;
Meaning: to scatter
KJV renders: scatter.

H0922.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (meaning to be empty);
Meaning: a vacuity, i.e. (superficially) an undistinguishable ruin
KJV renders: emptiness, void.

H0923.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (probably meaning to glisten);
Meaning: white marble or perhaps alabaster
KJV renders: red (marble).

H0924.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from 927;
Meaning: a hurry; only adverb, hastily
KJV renders: in haste.

H0925.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (meaning to be bright);
Meaning: shining
KJV renders: bright.

H0926.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to tremble inwardly (or palpitate), i.e. (figuratively) be (causative, make) (suddenly) alarmed or agitated; by implication to hasten anxiously
KJV renders: be (make) affrighted (afraid, amazed, dismayed, rash), (be, get, make) haste(-n, -y, -ily), (give) speedy(-ily), thrust out, trouble, vex.

H0927.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 926;
Meaning: to terrify, hasten
KJV renders: in haste, trouble.

H0928.strongs:
Origin: from 926;
Meaning: panic, destruction
KJV renders: terror, trouble.

H0929.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (probably meaning to be mute);
Meaning: properly, a dumb beast; especially any large quadruped or animal (often collective)
KJV renders: beast, cattle.

H0930.strongs:
Origin: in form a plural or 929, but really a singular of Egyptian derivation;
Meaning: a water-ox, i.e. the hippopotamus or Nile-horse
KJV renders: Behemoth.

H0931.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root apparently meaning to be thick;
Meaning: the thumb of the hand or great toe of the foot
KJV renders: thumb, great toe.

H0932.strongs:
Origin: an orthographical variation of 931;
Meaning: thumb, Bohan, an Israelite
KJV renders: Bohan.

H0933.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to be pale;
Meaning: white scurf
KJV renders: freckled spot.

H0934.strongs:
Origin: feminine active participle of the same as 925;
Meaning: a whitish spot on the skin
KJV renders: bright spot.

H0935.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to go or come (in a wide variety of applications)
KJV renders: abide, apply, attain, × be, befall, besiege, bring (forth, in, into, to pass), call, carry, × certainly, (cause, let, thing for) to come (against, in, out, upon, to pass), depart, × doubtless again, eat, employ, (cause to) enter (in, into, -tering, -trance, -try), be fallen, fetch, follow, get, give, go (down, in, to war), grant, have, × indeed, (in-) vade, lead, lift (up), mention, pull in, put, resort, run (down), send, set, × (well) stricken (in age), × surely, take (in), way.

H0936.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to disrespect
KJV renders: contemn, despise, × utterly.

H0937.strongs:
Origin: from 936;
Meaning: disrespect
KJV renders: contempt(-uously), despised, shamed.

H0938.strongs:
Origin: the same as 937;
Meaning: Buz, the name of a son of Nahor, and of an Israelite
KJV renders: Buz.

H0939.strongs:
Origin: feminine passive participle of 936;
Meaning: something scorned; an object of contempt
KJV renders: despised.

H0940.strongs:
Origin: patronymic from 938;
Meaning: a Buzite or descendant of Buz
KJV renders: Buzite.

H0941.strongs:
Origin: the same as 940;
Meaning: Buzi, an Israelite
KJV renders: Buzi.

H0942.strongs:
Origin: probably of Persian origin;
Meaning: Bavvai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Bavai.

H0943.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to involve (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: be entangled, (perplexed).

H0944.strongs:
Origin: for 2981;
Meaning: produce (of the earth, etc.)
KJV renders: food, stock.

H0945.strongs:
Origin: the same as 944 (in the sense of rain);
Meaning: Bul, the eighth Hebrew month
KJV renders: Bul.

H0946.strongs:
Origin: from 995; discretion;
Meaning: Bunah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Bunah.

H0947.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to trample (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: loath, tread (down, under (foot)), be polluted.

H0948.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (of the same form) meaning to bleach, i.e. (intransitive) be white;
Meaning: probably cotton (of some sort)
KJV renders: fine (white) linen.

H0949.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 948; shining;
Meaning: Botsets, a rock near Michmash
KJV renders: Bozez.

H0950.strongs:
Origin: feminine passive participle of an unused root (meaning to be hollow);
Meaning: emptiness (as adjective)
KJV renders: empty.

H0951.strongs:
Origin: properly, active participle from 1239 as denominative from 1241;
Meaning: a cattle-tender
KJV renders: herdman.

H0952.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to bore, i.e. (figuratively) examine
KJV renders: declare.

H0953.strongs:
Origin: from 952 (in the sense of 877);
Meaning: a pit hole (especially one used as a cistern or a prison)
KJV renders: cistern, dungeon, fountain, pit, well.

H0954.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to pale, i.e. by implication to be ashamed; also (by implication) to be disappointed or delayed
KJV renders: (be, make, bring to, cause, put to, with, a-) shamed(-d), be (put to) confounded(-fusion), become dry, delay, be long.

H0955.strongs:
Origin: feminine participle passive of 954;
Meaning: shame
KJV renders: shame.

H0956.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) apparent denominative from 1005;
Meaning: to lodge over night
KJV renders: pass the night.

H0957.strongs:
Origin: from 962;
Meaning: plunder
KJV renders: booty, prey, spoil(-ed).

H0958.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: probably to cleave
KJV renders: spoil.

H0959.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to disesteem
KJV renders: despise, disdain, contemn(-ptible), think to scorn, vile person.

H0960.strongs:
Origin: from 959;
Meaning: scorned
KJV renders: despise.

H0961.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 957;
Meaning: booty
KJV renders: prey, spoil.

H0962.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to plunder
KJV renders: catch, gather, (take) for a prey, rob(-ber), spoil, take (away, spoil), × utterly.

H0964.strongs:
Origin: from 959 and 3050; contempts of Jah;
Meaning: Bizjothjah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Bizjothjah.

H0965.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to lighten;
Meaning: a flash of lightning
KJV renders: flash of lightning.

H0966.strongs:
Origin: from 965; lightning;
Meaning: Bezek, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Bezek.

H0967.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to disperse
KJV renders: scatter.

H0968.strongs:
Origin: of Persian origin;
Meaning: Biztha, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV renders: Biztha.

H0969.strongs:
Origin: from 974;
Meaning: an assayer or metals
KJV renders: tower.

H0970.strongs:
Origin: or בָּחֻר; participle passive of 977;
Meaning: properly, selected, i.e. a youth (often collective)
KJV renders: (choice) young (man), chosen, × hole.

H0971.strongs:
Origin: another form of 975;
Meaning: a watch-tower of besiegers
KJV renders: tower.

H0972.strongs:
Origin: from 977;
Meaning: select
KJV renders: choose, chosen one, elect.

H0973.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to loath
KJV renders: abhor, get hastily (from the margin for 926).

H0974.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to test (especially metals); generally and figuratively, to investigate
KJV renders: examine, prove, tempt, try (trial).

H0975.strongs:
Origin: from 974 (in the sense of keeping a look-out);
Meaning: a watch-tower
KJV renders: tower.

H0976.strongs:
Origin: from 974;
Meaning: trial
KJV renders: tried.

H0977.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to try, i.e. (by implication) select
KJV renders: acceptable, appoint, choose (choice), excellent, join, be rather, require.

H0978.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 980 (by transposition);
Meaning: a Bacharumite or inhabitant of Bachurim
KJV renders: Baharumite.

H0979.strongs:
Origin: or בְּחוּרוֹת; feminine plural of 970; also (masculine plural) בְּחֻרִים;
Meaning: youth (collectively and abstractly)
KJV renders: young men, youth.

H0980.strongs:
Origin: or בַּחוּרִים; masculine plural of 970; young men;
Meaning: Bachurim, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Bahurim.

H0981.strongs:
Origin: or בָּטָה; a primitive root;
Meaning: to babble; hence, to vociferate angrily
KJV renders: pronounce, speak (unadvisedly).

H0982.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to hie for refuge (but not so precipitately as 2620); figuratively, to trust, be confident or sure
KJV renders: be bold (confident, secure, sure), careless (one, woman), put confidence, (make to) hope, (put, make to) trust.

H0983.strongs:
Origin: from 982;
Meaning: properly, a place of refuge; abstract, safety, both the fact (security) and the feeling (trust); often (adverb with or without preposition) safely
KJV renders: assurance, boldly, (without) care(-less), confidence, hope, safe(-ly, -ty), secure, surely.

H0984.strongs:
Origin: the same as 983;
Meaning: Betach, a place in Syria
KJV renders: Betah.

H0985.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 984;
Meaning: trust
KJV renders: confidence.

H0986.strongs:
Origin: from 982;
Meaning: trust
KJV renders: confidence, hope.

H0987.strongs:
Origin: feminine plural from 982;
Meaning: security
KJV renders: secure.

H0988.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to desist from labor
KJV renders: cease.

H0989.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 988;
Meaning: to stop
KJV renders: (cause, make to), cease, hinder.

H0990.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root probably meaning to be hollow;
Meaning: the belly, especially the womb; also the bosom or body of anything
KJV renders: belly, body, as they be born, within, womb.

H0991.strongs:
Origin: the same as 990;
Meaning: Beten. a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Beten.

H0992.strongs:
Origin: from 990;
Meaning: (only in plural) a pistachio-nut (from its form)
KJV renders: nut.

H0993.strongs:
Origin: probably plural from 992; hollows;
Meaning: Betonim, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Betonim.

H0994.strongs:
Origin: perhaps from 1158 (in the sense of asking); properly, a request; used only adverbially (always with 'my Lord');
Meaning: oh that!; with leave, or if it please
KJV renders: alas, O, oh.

H0995.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to separate mentally (or distinguish), i.e.(generally) understand
KJV renders: attend, consider, be cunning, diligently, direct, discern, eloquent, feel, inform, instruct, have intelligence, know, look well to, mark, perceive, be prudent, regard, (can) skill(-full), teach, think, (cause, make to, get, give, have) understand(-ing), view, (deal) wise(-ly, man).

H0998.strongs:
Origin: from 995;
Meaning: understanding
KJV renders: knowledge, meaning, × perfectly, understanding, wisdom.
